            { type: `tf`, q: `10) Higher video bit rate accommodate higher image quality`, a: 0, why: `Bit rate = bits per second of video. More bits per second means less compression (less data thrown away), so higher quality is possible at the cost of bandwidth/storage.`, key: `Old syllabus: not in your current lectures` }
